From d5d18dd00a8da7d26cb7fc36adb36113c7f1eb9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 00:42:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/19] Add the AeroDataBox seed adapter and record the live
 pilot

Tried against the real API on a free tier, which settled several things the
pricing page gets wrong or omits.  A FIDS call costs 2 units, not 1, and the
12-hour window persists through the Ultra plan, so a full month of the 58
Mexican airports is 6,960 units -- past the 5,000 of the cheap plan.  A window
longer than 12 hours returns an empty list rather than an error, and withLeg
must be set or a departure record carries no arrival airport and the route
cannot be recovered at all.  Both traps are now encoded rather than left to
the caller.

On the acceptance test the source passes the measure that matters: coverage
differs between carriers by 1.12x, against a 1.15x threshold and OpenSky's
2.8x.  Every flight carries an identified airline and 99% an arrival airport.
The automatic verdict is still REJECT because three small carriers are absent
and passenger coverage reaches 93.3%, both consistent with having sampled 40
of 58 airports on a single Tuesday; a full month resolves it.  Nothing is
published until a complete month returns ACCEPT.

Aeromexico and Aerolitoral share the AM code but are separate carriers in the
AFAC margin, so they are split by fleet.  Codeshares, freight operators and
foreign destinations are dropped by name rather than silently.

